-- title:
--   The ℓ-degeneracy roof is a curve over K
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a perfect field whose characteristic is $p$, and let $N,\ell$ be natural numbers, both nonzero, with $p \nmid N\ell$. Inside the Laurent series field $K((q))$ consider the intermediate field $\mathrm{charLDegeneracyRoof}\,K\,N\,\ell$ over $K$ generated by the four series `jqModC K`, `jqNModC K N`, `jqNModC K ℓ` and `jqNModC K (N*ℓ)`, i.e. the $q$-expansion $j(q)$ (the Laurent series $q^{-1}$ times the integral $j$-numerator series reduced into $K$) together with its substitutions $q \mapsto q^{N}$, $q \mapsto q^{\ell}$ and $q \mapsto q^{N\ell}$. The assertion is that this field $R$, viewed as an extension of $K$, satisfies [`AlgebraicCurve.IsCurveOver K R`](def/AlgebraicCurve_IsCurveOver.html#L15): every nonzero $f \in R$ admits a divisor $D$ of degree $0$ with $D(v) = \mathrm{ord}_v(f)$ at every place $v$ of $R/K$ (a place being a proper valuation subring of $R$ containing the image of $K$ whose ring is a principal ideal ring); each such place has residue field finite-dimensional over $K$; and the module of Kähler differentials $\Omega_{R/K}$ is free of rank one over $R$. The integer $\ell$ is not assumed prime here.
--
--   This provides the curve structure on the degeneracy roof $K(j(q),j(q^{N}),j(q^{\ell}),j(q^{N\ell}))$, the function field of the modular curve of level $N\ell$ in its $q$-expansion incarnation, so that divisors, trace bounds and fibres of places over it are available. It is used on the roof side of the supersingular Hecke computations, in particular in the comparison of Hecke divisors with fibre divisors under place specialisation.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_isCurveOver_charLDegeneracyRoof.lean

